---
import Section from '../components/content/Section.astro';
import {PageHero} from '../components/content/PageHero';
import {COMPANY_INFO} from '../data/companyData';
import {PRIVACY_POLICY_APPROVED_ON} from '../data/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const paragraph = 'text-sm text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl';
const link = 'text-lime-400 hover:text-lime-300 transition-colors';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy | VipraTech"
  description="How vipratech.in uses analytics and cookies, what it collects, and the choices you have."
  page={{type: 'privacy'}}
  crumbs={[{name: 'Privacy policy', path: '/privacy/'}]}
>
  <PageHero
    title="Privacy policy"
    subtitle={PRIVACY_POLICY_APPROVED_ON ? `Last updated ${PRIVACY_POLICY_APPROVED_ON}` : 'Draft'}
  />

  <Section title="Who we are">
    <p class={paragraph}>
      This website, vipratech.in, is run by {COMPANY_INFO.name}, {COMPANY_INFO.address}. For any privacy question or
      request, email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY_INFO.email}`} class={link}>{COMPANY_INFO.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="What this site collects">
    <p class={paragraph}>
      <strong class="text-white">Analytics.</strong> We use Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages
      and buttons people use: pages viewed, clicks on the booking and WhatsApp buttons, use-case pages viewed and the
      filters used in the use case library. Google Analytics sets cookies and records your approximate location,
      device and browser. We do not send it your name, email or phone number.
    </p>
    <p class={paragraph}>
      <strong class="text-white">Advertising.</strong> If we run Google Ads, the same Google tag tells us when someone
      who clicked one of our ads goes on to click "Book a 20-minute call".
    </p>
    <p class={paragraph}>
      <strong class="text-white">Visitors in the EEA, UK and Switzerland.</strong> Analytics and advertising cookies
      stay off until you accept them in the cookie banner. Until then, Google may receive basic signals without
      cookies, such as that a page was loaded. The banner stores your choice in a cookie for six months, and you can
      change it at any time with "Cookie settings" at the bottom of every page.
    </p>
    <p class={paragraph}>
      <strong class="text-white">Visitors elsewhere.</strong> Analytics is on by default. You can block cookies in your
      browser settings or install the
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class={link} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p class={paragraph}>
      <strong class="text-white">Fit diagnostic.</strong> The fit diagnostic on the homepage runs in your browser.
      Your answers are not sent to us unless you choose to send the email it prepares.
    </p>
    <p class={paragraph}>
      <strong class="text-white">When you contact us.</strong> If you email, call or message us, we use what you send
      only to reply and to discuss working together.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Other services">
    <p class={paragraph}>
      "Book a 20-minute call" opens Calendly and "WhatsApp us" opens WhatsApp. The booking link tells Calendly which
      page you came from. What you enter there is handled under Calendly's and WhatsApp's own privacy policies. The site
      is hosted on GitHub Pages, and GitHub may log visitors' IP addresses for security.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="How long we keep data">
    <p class={paragraph}>
      Google Analytics data is kept for the retention period set in our Google Analytics account. Emails and messages
      are kept while we are in touch with you and as long as the law requires afterwards.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Your rights">
    <p class={paragraph}>
      You can ask us to tell you what personal data we hold about you, to correct it or to delete it, and you can
      withdraw consent at any time. Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY_INFO.email}`} class={link}>{COMPANY_INFO.email}</a>
      and we will reply within 30 days. Depending on where you live, these rights come from India's Digital Personal
      Data Protection Act 2023, the EU or UK GDPR, or other law, and you can also complain to your data protection
      authority.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Changes">
    <p class={paragraph}>If we change this policy, we will update it on this page with the new date.</p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
